# ============================================================
# Claude / AI tooling
# ============================================================
.claude/settings.local.json

# Scratch file for a long commit message passed to `git commit -F`. A `git add -A`
# swept one into a commit once — it reached `main` but not the npm tarball, whose
# `files` list is `bin` + `tools`. Ignored so that cannot happen again.
.claude/commit-msg.txt

# Graphify
graphify-out/

# Scratchpad / temporary files
docs/scratchpad/

# ============================================================
# Node / CLI
# ============================================================
node_modules/

# TypeScript build artifacts. Nothing here emits — `tsc` is only ever a checker —
# but it still writes its incremental state, and `composite: true` in
# tsconfig.base.json means every project has an outDir whether it fills it or not.
cli/dist/
scripts/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Build output: tsup bundles cli/ into bin/, and bin/ is what npm publishes.
# Not committed — unlike the authored plugins/ tree and the marketplace manifest
# generated from it, which are meant to be read and diffed. A bundle diff is
# noise, and `i:build` regenerates it before every publish.
bin/

# Working notes and session handoffs — personal state, not the team's.
#
# docs/memory/ splits by audience: `decisions`, `planning`, `gaps` and
# `problems` are the team's and stay committed; `handoff`, `doctor` and `runs`
# are one developer's state and are not. All three are listed whether or not
# they exist right now — they are written by a command, so the first run that
# creates one would otherwise commit personal state.
docs/memory/handoff/
docs/memory/doctor/
docs/memory/runs/

# A developer's own Cursor config, if they adapt these plugins for Cursor by the
# prompt route. That is a personal choice rather than the project's, and this repo
# ships nothing Cursor-specific any more.
.cursor/

# The authoring machine's develop-tracking marketplace, written by
# `mise run plugins:marketplace` alongside the published manifest. One machine's
# local state: it exists so the author can run the working tree rather than the
# last release. Untracked because a second file in the tree declaring the
# marketplace name `virajp-plugins` is a footgun on the branch users read, and
# because regenerating it is one command. `--check` reports it absent rather
# than failing — see `.claude/docs/dev-marketplace.md`.
.dev-marketplace/
